WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.589 line:91%
Chapter 20. Test 2: students think, talk, and try to beat their Test 1.

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:17.188 line:91%
Test 1 is calm: no speed points, and no podium. It only shows what to teach. Test 2 is the game: each student tries to beat their Test 1.

00:00:17.654 --> 00:00:20.770 line:91%
After you teach, press "Start Test 2".

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:32.926 line:91%
Start the first question. Lina answers.

00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:43.605 line:91%
Then the phone asks: "How sure are you?" Guessing, quite sure, or very sure. Students learn to check their own thinking.

00:00:44.056 --> 00:00:51.146 line:91%
About half the class is right? The "Talk and answer again" button turns blue. That is the best moment to talk.

00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:57.987 line:91%
Press it. Students talk to the student next to them for one minute: "I think it's… because…".

00:00:58.445 --> 00:01:07.785 line:91%
Press "Answer again". The same question opens. The first answer counts in the results. A right second answer gets extra game points.

00:01:08.238 --> 00:01:14.047 line:91%
Press "Reveal answer". Your phone shows "Why?": the right sentence, and a short rule.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:22.392 line:91%
You also see what talking changed, and how many students were sure but wrong. Press "Who?" to see their names.

00:01:22.851 --> 00:01:29.193 line:91%
On the phone: "Talking helped: now it's right!" Students who are still wrong see the reason why.

00:01:29.652 --> 00:01:36.453 line:91%
Here we jump to the end. Press "Finish test". Test 2 has the podium, with music and confetti.

00:01:56.198 --> 00:02:03.076 line:91%
Each phone shows: "You beat your Test 1!" The big screen shows how many students beat their Test 1.

00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:11.176 line:91%
Then the phones ask about today's goal again: "And now? Can you do it?" The board shows the class before and after.

00:02:11.642 --> 00:02:21.556 line:91%
Next class, start with the Warm-up: a few quick questions from earlier lessons, about the skills the class found hardest. No points, no podium.

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:27.897 line:91%
At the end, it shows what the class still remembers, compared with last time.
